-- ranges that overlap and ranges that do not
a holds bytes 0 to 9
b, bytes 5 to 14: held by another
b, bytes 10 to 19: taken
b, shared, bytes 0 to 4: held by another
a again, the range it holds: taken
-- giving up part of a range
b, shared, bytes 0 to 4: taken
a, shared beside it: taken
a, exclusive over b's shared lock: held by another
b, bytes 5 to 9, which a kept: held by another
-- to the end of the file, and past it
a, from byte 15 on: held by another
b gave up everything
a, from byte 15 on: taken
b, bytes 1000 to 1009, beyond the file: held by another
b, bytes 20 to 29, beyond the file: held by another
-- a thread waits for a range
while b holds part of it, the waiter has the range: false
after b let go the waiter returned 1
a, the waiter's range after its file was closed: taken
b, the same range after a's file was closed: taken
-- a lock needs the file open its way
exclusive, on a file open for reading: InvalidInput
shared, on the same file: taken
shared, on a file open for writing: InvalidInput
exclusive, on the same file: taken
cleaned up
